# Secrets: the UniFi and plug passwords, the SMTP password, and the UI
# password hash. Wildcarded because the exact name was not the risk -
# config.json.bak and config.local.json are what someone makes while
# debugging, and neither was ignored. Note the TRAILING wildcard: a
# pattern of config*.json does NOT match config.json.bak, because the
# name has to end in .json. Tested, not assumed. The example file is
# re-included: it holds placeholders only and must stay tracked.
config*.json*

# The concrete systemd unit, with your account and paths in it. Copy
# office-fan-controller.service.example and edit. Same reason as the
# config file: the example is the tracked one.
office-fan-controller.service
!config.example.json

# The virtual environment the README tells you to create. Python's own
# venv module writes venv/.gitignore containing "*", so a venv made
# that way already hides itself - which is why this was missed. A venv
# made with virtualenv, or with an older Python, does not, and then
# every clean install reports itself as MODIFIED in the version footer
# because the dirty check counts untracked files. Found by review of
# e91cbb0 against a checkout where the self-ignore was absent.
venv/
.venv/
env/

# Runtime state and vendored dependencies
history.json
daily.json
events.json
# Every persister writes through one of these; naming them individually
# meant fault.json.tmp was missed when the fault file was added.
*.json.tmp
*.log
libs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
fault.json
restart.request
manual-off.pending
